    <string name="help">Help</string>
    <string name="help_audio_quality">Opus and AAC sound transparent to most listeners at 128–160 kbps stereo. Speech can go much lower.</string>
    <string name="help_b1">Pick a video, choose a preset or a size target, and start. The app analyses the file and picks hardware encoding when the device supports your settings, otherwise software.</string>
    <string name="help_b2">Constant quality keeps quality steady and lets size vary. Target size computes the bitrate from the size you want; very small targets on long videos look bad, and the app warns before starting.</string>
    <string name="help_b3">Hardware encoders are fast and power-efficient but give less control. Software encoders are slower and offer more settings. Automatic picks hardware when it can do exactly what you asked.</string>
    <string name="help_b4">Encode a preview to see the real result on a short segment, measure size and PSNR/SSIM, and compare it side by side with the original.</string>
    <string name="help_b5">The queue keeps running in the background with a notification. Jobs pause when the device gets hot or (if you enabled it) when it is not charging. You can pause, resume, reorder and cancel jobs.</string>
    <string name="help_b6">Outputs go to Movies/Compressed by default. The original is never changed unless you explicitly enable “Replace original”.</string>
    <string name="help_b7">If a job fails, the report explains why and what to change. Diagnostics shows codec support on this device.</string>
    <string name="help_bframes">B-frames improve compression. Some hardware encoders ignore this setting.</string>
    <string name="help_denoise">Removing noise lets the encoder spend bits on detail. Strong settings can smear texture.</string>
    <string name="help_engine">Hardware: fast and power-efficient, fewer controls. Software: slower, more control, more consistent results across devices.</string>
    <string name="help_h1">Getting started</string>
    <string name="help_h2">Quality vs. target size</string>
    <string name="help_h3">Hardware vs. software</string>
    <string name="help_h4">Previews and comparison</string>
    <string name="help_h5">Background queue</string>
    <string name="help_h6">Where files are saved</string>
    <string name="help_h7">When something goes wrong</string>
    <string name="help_size_strategy">Choose what drives the file size: quality, a target size or a bitrate.</string>
    <string name="help_two_pass">Two-pass analyses the whole video first for more accurate size targets. It roughly doubles the encoding time.</string>
    <string name="help_vfr">Phone recordings often have variable frame rate. Keeping it avoids duplicated or dropped frames.</string>
